  "description": "BAVVUR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H104 Dy8 N24 O44,12(C2 H3 N1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.971-3.982 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.99-116.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C140H152Dy8N36O50. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
